      <description>&lt;h1 id=&#34;tradingagents&#34;&gt;TradingAgents&lt;/h1&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;This post will analyze the TradingAgents research paper and its associated code.&#xA;TradingAgents leverages a multi-agent framework to simulate a professional trading firm with distinct roles.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The system is built using Python and the &lt;code&gt;LangGraph&lt;/code&gt; library to orchestrate the interactions between agents in a structured workflow.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;langchain-and-langgraph&#34;&gt;LangChain and LangGraph&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;LangChain and LangGraph are Python frameworks for building applications powered by LLMs. LangGraph is an orchestration engine for complex, stateful agent workflows.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
